[Music]  I'm Alvin kai-lan chef/owner of eggslut  a boy unit 120 and our new pop up here  in New York City called chefs club  counter our breakfast sandwich is kind  of like your master's degree in  breakfast sandwiches it's just all one  crazy gooey sandwich and I think when  you eat an egg sandwich and you take a  bite out of it you want it to be  something memorable that you have for  the rest of the day the way we cook the  Fairfax is always with a cold pan crack  cold eggs into the cold pan throw a nub  of butter and steer it before you even  put it on the heat and once you see that  the yolks and the whites have created  somewhat of a uniform color that's what  you want to throw it onto the heat we  use a spatula so that it doesn't like  agitate the proteins and the egg so it  comes out naturally velvety when you're  mixing it you're scraping the bottom of  the pan so that you're folding the eggs  over so you're creating almost like  layers of egg when you're cooking it in  the pan it starts to peel off the pan  and when it starts to like not get loose  and it just starts to like stay together  the eggs are basically telling you we're  done  [Music]  chives and eggs like are so amazing  together it's like having cheese or  peanut butter and jelly I literally use  it instead of pepper when it's not  plenty more taking out of the pan  because the pans hot so to keep cooking  it and it's gonna ruin that last 25  minutes that you tried making amazing  eggs you could have the most expensive  ingredients in between two pieces of  bread but if the bread is not perfectly  warm or cooked it ruins the whole thing  we pair it with sriracha mayo and then  you know we had that really nice melted  cheese and we do a caramelized onion let  me cook it for eight hours  low and slow so it brings up the natural  sweetness at the end of the day once  it's like all put together and you're  like whoa this is this is actually  really really good and I think that  that's really why i